Description: XDJ hardware/behavior tweaks (bar markers, controller reconnect, tempo sync)
 1. Rekordbox-style bar markers: small red triangles at the top and bottom
    of the scrolling waveform on the first beat of each bar (both the
    QPainter and the allshader/QOpenGL beat renderers). The rekordbox ANLZ
    importer now anchors the beat grid on the first beat numbered "1"
    (rekordbox numbers beats 1-4 within a bar; Mixxx previously discarded
    this and could anchor mid-bar).
 2. Controller auto-reconnect: PortMidi controllers count consecutive
    read/write errors and report themselves disconnected; a 5 s watchdog in
    ControllerManager reopens enabled controllers that died or were
    (re)plugged, using the same rescan path as the preferences dialog.
    A controller that is enabled in the preferences but unplugged causes a
    periodic rescan until it returns; disable it in the preferences to stop.
 3. Pioneer DDJ-400 mapping: on track load the deck's tempo jumps to the
    physical tempo fader position (cached from fader movements and the
    startup position query SysEx), applied 200 ms after load to let Mixxx's
    own speed/pitch reset run first. Soft takeover then resumes with the
    internal value matching the fader, eliminating the dead slider until it
    crossed its old position.
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
